{"id":28876437854311,"type":"album","name":"Pretty On The Inside","artist":"Hole","year":1991,"weight":22,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710701.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-f47199f1-a6fb-45fb-97fd-cee5472ef9de/mbid-f47199f1-a6fb-45fb-97fd-cee5472ef9de-30662858952.jpg","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"Fm_sOuQEmZk","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/335Wo8YySOsJdc0QV9ANvK","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_k1MJlPnkzuxwZqpgh_UYBvdCD7GKlAVb0"},"desc":"With Sonic Youth's bassist Kim Gordon and Gumball's leader Don Fleming in charge of production, the studio work took only four days. Courtney Love gargled whiskey and smoked in excess during the recording sessions to give a raw edge to her vocals. She and lead guitarist Eric Erlandson were greatly influenced by punk and noise rock when making the album, and the chaotic guitar riffs combined with Love's disturbing lyrics and wild screaming showcase this. Riffs from Neil Young and Bauhaus songs are present in two songs on the album, admittedly lifted verbatim by Erlandson and Love. The album was ."},"artist_ref":{"id":127336684677400,"name":"Hole","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/HoleSXSW2010%28wide%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":3782,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":32992220995517,"type":"genre","name":"Grunge","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1361,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"}],"lists":[{"id":128252860635986,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Grunge","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":74,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","src":"charts","grp":"Scaruffi","list_year":null,"rank":764,"year":1991,"note":null,"total":1406,"scaruffi":7.0}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This was the debut record for Hole, released in September 1991. It was notably co-produced by Kim Gordon of Sonic Youth and Don Fleming, who was known for his work with Dinosaur Jr. and other indie groups. Though not an immediate hit, it eventually garnered cult favorite status. \"the result was a 1991 record entitled Pretty on the Inside, co-produced by Kim and Don Fleming, a guy known for his work with dinosaur Jr. and a ton of other indie groups.\"","year":1991,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90's Part 2B: Front Women","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Eo32mAZd8DI"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":28876437854311,"artist":"Hole","artist_id":127336684677400,"title":"Pretty On The Inside","year":1991,"ess":0,"yt":"Fm_sOuQEmZk","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Foxcore y riot grrrls","scene_id":222372523664182,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#foxcore","chapters":["Sección 6.10"],"pages":[[1,267,null]]}],"others":[{"id":255659385469394,"type":"album","name":"Live Through This","year":1994,"weight":39},{"id":17499009062790,"type":"album","name":"Celebrity Skin","year":1998,"weight":16},{"id":198201009070335,"type":"song","name":"Gold Dust Woman","year":1996,"weight":9},{"id":128648958920087,"type":"song","name":"Miss World","year":1994,"weight":9},{"id":199851648255436,"type":"album","name":"My Body the Hand Grenade","year":1997,"weight":7},{"id":72447189478669,"type":"song","name":"Teenage Horde","year":1991,"weight":7},{"id":37531559149004,"type":"song","name":"Asking for It","year":1994,"weight":7},{"id":600006631314,"type":"song","name":"Violet","year":1995,"weight":7},{"id":241242354952496,"type":"album","name":"New Hole Album","year":1994,"weight":4},{"id":205558945356371,"type":"song","name":"Asking For It (Undetermined Vintage)","year":null,"weight":4},{"id